| `agents.protected_names.<name>` | string | sixteen names or globs, each with its reason: `AGENT.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, the three names make reads (`GNUmakefile`, `makefile`, `Makefile`), `conftest.py`, git's `.gitignore` and `.gitattributes`, and the frontend gates and their tests: `eslint.config.js`, `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `playwright.config.ts`, `tsconfig*.json`, `vitest.config.ts`, `*.test.*` and `*.spec.*` | a bare file name or an `fnmatch` glob over one (no `/`, not `.` or `..`) mapped to a non-blank reason; at least one entry | `scripts/apply_refactor.py` (`load_policy`, `protected_by`) | Refuses an agent edit to a file whose name it matches in any directory, case-folded; it wins over `agents.editable_names`. | a whole directory: `agents.protected_paths` | always |
